{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/195930-true-fae-and-their-contracts","id":195930,"title":"True Fae and their contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-12T19:19:02-07:00","id":195930,"title":"True Fae and their contracts","content":"So we're doing a higher level game and I'm letting a player play a true fae. How does using contracts work for the True Fae with their flexible contract like Arcana? I read it but didn't quite get it. Examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T19:37:12-07:00","id":195950,"title":"","content":"In general, a good way to look at is to treat it as being able to do anything appropriate to the power level, like they're arcana of a very specific thematic.<br /> <br /> If you do have Mage, what I'd do is let them cast any spell that fits a Contract's thematics from any Arcana. For instance, if a True Fae has Contracts of Hearth, you could give them all of the luck based Fate spells up to the level they have (Which, yes, is most of them, but Fate is pretty perfect for gentry to be easily able to manipulate with a single contract), and then add some other similar things like Perfect Timing from Time 1. Similarly, Contracts of Artifice might give you access to appropriate Matter spells with regards to devices, but also the couple of Death spells that let you destroy or degrade them, the Platonic Mechanism Fate 3 spell if they have 3+ dots, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T23:08:48-07:00","id":196051,"title":"","content":"I'd probably buff up powers I wouldn't let them be as flexible as mages but I'd give them very strong powers unique to the fae rather than generic ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T08:54:57-07:00","id":196319,"title":"","content":"First off, how in God's name did you end up letting a player play an Other? This isn't a criticism at all, I'm genuinely curious to hear how that came about.<br /> <br /> In my games, I assume any True Fae has a functionally limitless number of dots in the Goblin Vow Merit from <i>Rites Of Spring</i>, connected to whatever purviews fit the Other in question. This gives you a lot of flexibility with their powers without letting them go so absolutely wild that the players have no chance of confronting them successfully. Keep in mind the power level of a True Fae when working out Goblin Vows too-what might be a Greater task for a less-powerful Changeling might count as Medial to a being that channels Wyrd as naturally as humans eat and sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:29:16-07:00","id":196775,"title":"","content":"I did something similar to QuatreVingts, and also had quite a lot of reskinned Contracts/Clauses that used the same mechanics but with the aesthetics altered to be more appropriate for the Fae in question (for example, one Fae had Contracts of Endless Summer, but with the dice pools tweaked and the aesthetics changed to be more to do with flesh and ovens. I called it the Contract of Cooking, not that I ever told the players that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T17:59:39-07:00","id":197290,"title":"","content":"There's a whole section in Autumn Nightmares that gives rules for creating True Fae. They're designed more for storyteller use than the players but there's some really good rules and examples for the level of power and mindset the Gentry possess. As for Contracts I personally would say use them as they're presented in the Changeling core rulebook. The True Fae only possess god like power over the forces of the world in their own demesne in Arcadia. Outside of it they're bound to the same rules most Changelings are susceptible to, the only difference is that they start off with a crap ton more Contracts and dots in Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T21:23:07-07:00","id":197430,"title":"","content":"Well the story is set in a Fantasy based game kinda like from Mirror's and the player I question only has a name no titles and is starting with Changeling dots lay out, but with Wyrd 4. He just has True Fae powers like what the hook suggest about using contracts like Arcana. He's essential playing his Actor part of the a true fae cut off from his realm trying to get his realm back I guess it's almost like playing a Arch Mage, like a tier 4 Changeling game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}